{"id": "tea:sunyatasaptati:1", "source": "src:sunyatasaptati", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Arising, abiding and ceasing, existence and non-existence, the inferior, middling and excellent are spoken of by the Buddha in accordance with worldly convention, not in reality.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:two-truths"], "terms": ["trm:vyavahara"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sunyatasaptati:64-65", "source": "src:sunyatasaptati", "location": {"ref": "64-65"}, "paraphrase": "The Teacher called ignorance the conceiving of things born from causes and conditions as real; from it the twelve links arise. When one sees well that things are empty one is not deluded; ignorance ceases and the twelve links cease.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:avidya"], "concepts": ["cpt:twelve-links-in-madhyamaka"], "obstacles": ["obs:svabhava-graha"], "notes": "Verse numbers from memory.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
